# BUG-380: a Python-shaped trailing colon on any block header (`if x:`, `for x in xs:`,
# `while c:`, `def f():`, `else:`, `class Foo:`) hit five different parser-internal
# messages depending on which parse path swallowed the colon. One check, one message that
# points at the indented-body form and the `header: stmt` one-liner.
def main()
    if true:
        print(1)
